   "gap": "thm:p15-absolute-iterated-series (proved=annex:p15.absolute-iterated-series): the series half connects the corollary's sums to Fubini's integrals only through two bare assertions, 'The assumed sum is the first iterated absolute integral, because integration with respect to kappa is summation' (handbook/annex/p15/product-measures.tex lines 514-515) and 'counting-measure integration of that integrable section equals the sum' (lines 520-521). Neither identity is derived in the proof or established on the route: that the integral against counting measure on N+ of a nonnegative g equals sum_n g(n), and the signed version for an absolutely summable section (thm:p15-expectation-law-integral covers only countable atomic probability spaces). Owed: written derivation of these counting-measure identities and the three identifications they carry: the hypothesis sum_n int|f_n| with Fubini's iterated-absolute premise, H with the section absolute integral (516-518), and S with Fubini's second section-integral function (522-523). handbook/annex/p15/product-measures.tex is an editable host of this packet.",
